// Pine has no QUALIFIED tuple destructuring. TV reads the qualifier as the
// variable NAME: ONE error at the keyword, `""var"" cannot be used as a
// variable or function name.`, and nothing on the names. Same for `varip`.
//
// This probe carries the half the regression fixture cannot. The fix has two
// effects - the right message at the right column, AND recovering through the
// destructuring so the names stay declared - and the second is only visible in
// the VALIDATION channel, which the fixture harness skips entirely once
// parsing fails. Before the fix the CLI emitted three errors here: the wrong
// message at 5:5, plus `Undefined variable 'x'` and `'y'` at the plot below.
//
//     pine-lint -H <this file>     -> expect exactly 2 errors, both at col 1
//
// `const [x, y]` is NOT this shape - TV answers it with `Mismatched input "x"
// expecting set "]"`, reading `const [` as a type annotation. Unhandled.
//@version=6
indicator("qualified destructuring")
f() =>
    [1, 2]
var [x, y] = f()
varip [p, q] = f()
plot(x + y + p + q)
